From e45a07796c01233f8d713f4230af02693d5006a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ship the licence of the bundled liblz4 in the wheel

3.29.12 adds the cassandra.cython_lz4 extension, which links liblz4
dynamically, so auditwheel copies the system liblz4.so.1 into
scylla_driver.libs/ next to libev: every manylinux wheel now also
redistributes liblz4 in binary form. The LZ4 library is BSD-2-Clause and its
terms require the copyright notice to travel with the binary.

As with LICENSE.libev, pyproject.toml declares no license-files, so
setuptools' default LICEN[CS]E* root glob picks the new file up. The text is
lib/LICENSE from lz4 1.9.4, the version the manylinux image packages; it is
unchanged in 1.10.0.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 LICENSE.lz4 | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.lz4

diff --git a/LICENSE.lz4 b/LICENSE.lz4
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..04c61c61
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.lz4
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+The liblz4 shared library the cassandra.cython_lz4 extension links against
+is redistributed inside the binary wheel. liblz4 is not part of this project
+and carries the licence below; the driver's own licence is in LICENSE.
